Item 8: EDID fixes (Marcelo, Chris). revision 1. ONE DECISION NEEDED (the detailed timing).

Uncommitted on top of 575a3484204f (series head, pushed). item8.diff = `git diff`, covering
dcp-panel-edid.{c,h}, dcp-panel-edid-test.c, iomfb.c and apple-dcp/rate.py.

FINDINGS AND VALIDATION
Evidence: the panel's live EDID from the running branch kernel (/sys/class/drm/card2-eDP-1/
edid), decoded with edid-decode 1.32.0 and di-edid-decode (libdisplay-info 0.3.0) on the M3. A
host dump of dcp_panel_edid_block() reproduces it byte for byte. The dumper is a scratch tool:
the .c file is built with stub headers and struct edid is taken from include/drm/drm_edid.h.
1. gamma byte 0x17 = 0 decodes as "Gamma: 1.00". Real.
2. year: "Made in: 1990" (byte 0x11 = 0), and libdisplay-info reports "Year set to reserved
   value". Real.
3. no detailed timing first: edid-decode fails with "Standard Timings: Missing preferred timing";
   libdisplay-info fails 4x with "The first byte descriptor must contain the preferred timing".
   Real. libdisplay-info also fails "White-point coordinates are unset" (Marcelo's point that
   libdisplay-info would flag the block).
4. dcp_panel_edid_update() wrote the DT panel size into display_info, while
   dcp_update_connector_dimensions() prefers the firmware's dcp->width_mm/height_mm. Real (code
   reading: dcp.c:585-598 against dcp-panel-edid.c). On the J516C the two differ: the firmware
   gives 346x216 mm (notch rows hidden), the node 346x223.
5. the new dcp_get_modes() branch leaves drm_edid_firmware_derived as it was. Real (code
   reading): after an earlier firmware-derived publication the flag stays true.
6. KUnit fixture WARNING. Real. KUnit baseline at 575a3484 on the M3 (kunit.py --arch=arm64 in
   QEMU/KVM, chroot LLVM, aurora.kunitconfig, then run-kunit.py --check-only):
   "1541 pass, 0 fail, 3 skip; 1 kernel splats", with the difference "kernel splat
   drivers/gpu/drm/drm_connector.c:drm_connector_init_only in
   apple-dcp-panel-edid.panel_edid_update_keeps_the_size_in_mm: 1 seen, 0 expected" (test.log:
   WARNING drm_connector.c:236). Output: ~/Projects/build-out/kunit-stack177/base575/.

FIX (done)
- Gamma: byte 0x17 = 0x78, nominal 2.2. Why 2.2: these panels are P3 wide-colour panels (public
  spec), and Display P3 uses the sRGB transfer function, which a gamma of 2.2 approximates. The
  EDID gamma byte is nominal; 0xff would point at an extension, as Marcelo noted.
- Model year: week 0xff (the year byte is the model year), year 2023 - 1990 = 33. The year
  comes from a table keyed on the panel model ({ "J516", 2023 }: the 16-inch MacBook Pro with
  M3 Pro or M3 Max came out in 2023), filled into struct dcp_panel_id.model_year by
  dcp_panel_id_from_compatible(). dcp_panel_edid_block() refuses a year EDID 1.4 reserves
  (< 2006) or cannot hold, so a model with no known year gets no block (the dcp_get_modes()
  path then warns once, as for any update failure). Only the J516C reaches this path
  (iomfb_v14_7_base_edid()).
- dimensions: dcp_panel_edid_update() no longer touches display_info (the EDID update sets it
  from the block's whole centimetres). The dcp_get_modes() branch calls the existing
  dcp_update_connector_dimensions() before the update, so the block is sized from the same
  source (firmware first, then the node), and again after it, to give the connector back its
  millimetres. The firmware width/height stay the single source of truth.
- drm_edid_firmware_derived = false in that branch.
- KUnit fixture: connector funcs .reset/.atomic_duplicate_state/.atomic_destroy_state = the
  drm_atomic_helper_connector_* helpers (the KUnit DRM device is atomic). Test asserts:
  gamma 0x78, mfg_week 0xff, mfg_year 33, id.model_year 2023, a model without a year gets 0,
  a block with model_year 2005 is refused. The update case is renamed
  panel_edid_update_publishes_the_block and asserts 350x220 after the update (the block's cm;
  the mm restore is now the caller's).
- apple-dcp/rate.py (publication-hpd harness): stub dcp_update_connector_dimensions() (asserts,
  since the H17P scenarios never reach the branch) and display_info width_mm/height_mm in the
  mock connector.

