DECISION NEEDED: THE DETAILED TIMING (and, tied to it, the colour characteristics)
The task asks for a DTD of 3456x2234@120 with the timing 3456 3464 3496 3536 / 2234 2352 2360
2456 and the pixel clock from 120 Hz. That timing CANNOT be encoded in an EDID detailed timing
descriptor, for two independent reasons:
- pixel clock: 3536 x 2456 x 120 = 1,042,145,280 Hz. The DTD clock field is 16 bits in 10 kHz
  units, at most 655.35 MHz. Any native-resolution timing at 120 Hz is at least
  3456 x 2234 x 120 = 926 MHz, so this holds even with reduced blanking.
- vertical front porch: 2352 - 2234 = 118 lines. The DTD field is 6 bits, at most 63.
(The DCP mode line on this boot is "3456x2160": 120 1042130 3456 3464 3496 3536 2160 2278 2360
2456, the same porches with 74 notch rows hidden.)
Prototypes (raw bytes from the new block, decoded on the M3; ~/aurora-test/edid-dump/proto/):
  (a) + P3 primaries and D65 white only: edid-decode FAIL (missing preferred timing);
      libdisplay-info FAIL (first descriptor), with the white-point failure gone.
  (b) (a) + a DisplayID 2.0 extension with a Type VII timing holding the exact 120 Hz timing
      (extensions = 1): still FAIL in both decoders; both require the preferred timing in the
      base block's first descriptor (edid-decode adds "Missing DisplayID Display Parameters
      Data Block").
  (c) (a) + a first-descriptor DTD of 3456x2234 at 60 Hz: htotal 3536 and the horizontal
      porches exact, vtotal 2456 and vsync width 8 exact, vertical front porch 48 instead of 118,
      clock 521.07 MHz (3536 x 2456 x 60); the monitor name moved to descriptor 1: edid-decode
      "EDID conformity: PASS" (one warning, no native resolution); libdisplay-info no
      failures.
So a conformant base block needs (c)-like content: a DTD at a rate whose clock fits (at most
75 Hz with these totals) and a vertical front porch of at most 63, i.e. a timing that is NOT
the firmware's. On this platform it is descriptive only: dcp_get_modes() publishes the
firmware's modes and never adds modes from this EDID (it calls drm_edid_connector_update(),
not drm_edid_connector_add_modes()). A fixed 60 Hz refresh at full resolution is a published
option of this panel; 60 Hz with these exact porches is not known.
Options:
  D1: (c). A 60 Hz DTD, porches as close to the firmware's as the DTD holds (vfp 63, vback
      151, or 48/166 as prototyped), features bit 1 left clear (the DTD does not carry the
      preferred refresh rate), plus P3/D65 chromaticity, with a comment saying it is the base
      block's encodable timing, not the firmware's. Both decoders pass.
  D2: no DTD. Keep gamma and model year (and optionally the P3/D65 chromaticity), and reply to
      Marcelo with the two encoding limits above. Both decoders keep the first-descriptor
      failure.
  D3: D1 or D2 plus a DisplayID extension carrying the true 120 Hz timing. This adds an
      extension block for information nothing here reads; not recommended.
My recommendation: D1 with vfp 63 / vback 151 (the least-changed vertical timing) and the
chromaticity. It meets what Marcelo asked for (a timing in the first descriptor, a block that
libdisplay-info accepts), without claiming the 120 Hz native timing, and the comment and the
commit message say so. If you choose D2, I drop the chromaticity unless you want it: it is a
P3 claim from the public spec, not a measurement.

PLANNED COMMIT (after the decision): one fixup into 4b32d3e6 "drm/apple: give the J516C panel
a base EDID" (the commit that adds the builder, the test, the dcp_get_modes() branch and the
rate.py stubs). Message: replace "no manufacture date, no colour primaries, no timings"
wording to match the chosen option; state gamma 2.2 with the P3 reason, and the model year.
Then the per-commit build, apple-dcp run.sh and KUnit at the head.

============================================================================================
revision 2: user decision D4 (60 Hz base-block DTD + DisplayID extension with the 120 Hz
timing; D1 as fallback). D4 PASSES both decoders, so D4 is used.

Correction to revision 1: 3536 x 2456 x 120 = 1,042,129,920 Hz (= the DCP's 1042130 kHz), not
1,042,145,280; at 60 Hz it is 521,064,960 Hz (DTD field 52106). The limits are unchanged.

PROTOTYPING (M3, ~/aurora-test/edid-dump/d4/, both decoders)
- DisplayID 1.3 Type I timing: edid-decode PASS only with product type 1; libdisplay-info FAIL
  ("Padding: Contains non-zero bytes"). Rejected.
- DisplayID 2.0 Type VII alone: edid-decode FAIL ("Base Block has no product type" with 0; with
  a use case it requires a Display Parameters block). libdisplay-info PASS.
- DisplayID 2.0, primary use 0x02 "generic display", Display Parameters (0x21) + Type VII:
  BOTH PASS, with no warnings (even "No Native Video Resolution" is gone). Field encodings were
  probed against edid-decode's decoding (product type, feature bits, colour/technology byte,
  gamma position, IEEE half-float luminance).

FIX (item8.diff, revision 2: the revision 1 fixes plus the following)
dcp-panel-edid.{c,h}:
- The model table carries the native timing from the DCP mode line with all rows shown:
  J516 = 1042130 kHz, 3456 3464 3496 3536 / 2234 2352 2360 2456 (dcp_panel_id.timing).
- dcp_panel_edid_block() is replaced by dcp_panel_edid_build(id, w_mm, h_mm, u8[2 * 128]).
  A model without a year or a valid timing gets no EDID (-EINVAL).
- The base block has P3/D65 chromaticity (10-bit), gamma 0x78 and model year 2023. Descriptor 0
  is a DTD with the panel's geometry at 60 Hz: clock 52106 (521.06 MHz); horizontal 3456/80
  blank, porch 8, sync 32; vertical 2234/222 blank, porch 63 (the field's maximum; the panel's
  is 118), sync 8, back porch 151; size 346x216 mm, the connector's (firmware) size, the same
  source as the cm fields; positive syncs. Descriptor 1 is the monitor name, descriptors 2-3 are
  dummies. Features bit 1 is clear. extensions = 1.
- The DisplayID 2.0 extension (tag 0x70): use case 0x02, generic display. Display Parameters:
  346.0x216.0 mm, 3456x2234 native, left to right and top to bottom, CIE 1931, speakers not
  integrated, P3/D65 (12-bit), luminance not known (left 0; edid-decode prints 0 as 0.000031
  cd/m^2), colour depth not given, active-matrix LCD, gamma 2.2. Type VII timing: 1042130 kHz,
  preferred, aspect from the pixels, the exact DCP porches, positive syncs. Section checksum
  and block checksum both filled.
- dcp_panel_edid_update() builds both blocks (256 bytes, kmalloc) and publishes them with
  drm_edid_connector_update(). It still adds no mode.
- The file comment says that the base DTD is 60 Hz because the 16-bit pixel-clock field (at most
  655.35 MHz) and the 6-bit front porch cannot hold the 120 Hz timing, that the extension
  carries the real 120 Hz timing, and that the DRM modes stay the DCP firmware's.
KUnit (dcp-panel-edid-test.c; J516_H_MM is now 216, the firmware's height):
- panel_id_from_compatible: timing clock 1042130 and vtotal 2456; j999 gets no year and no
  timing.
- panel_edid_parses_with_make_product_and_size: also P3 red and D65 white (10-bit),
  extensions == 1, both blocks sum to 0.
- panel_edid_has_no_serial_and_no_timings is renamed to panel_edid_timings_are_the_panels. It
  checks every DTD field above, features bit 1 clear, one name and no serial or range
  descriptors, and the DisplayID header (0x70, 2.0, use case 2, length 55, section checksum),
  Display Parameters (size in 0.1 mm, native pixels, gamma) and all Type VII fields against the
  DCP mode line.
- panel_edid_refuses_a_size_it_cannot_hold: also clock 0 is refused.
- panel_edid_update_publishes_the_block: the blob is 256 bytes, and probed_modes stays empty
  after the update (no mode from the EDID).

