PLANNED COMMIT: one fixup into 4b32d3e6 "drm/apple: give the J516C panel a base EDID", reworded
to "drm/apple: give the J516C panel an EDID". The body says: the base block names the panel
(APP, J516), gives its size from the connector (firmware first, then the node), model year 2023,
gamma 2.2 and P3/D65 colour; its detailed timing is the panel's geometry at 60 Hz, because the
EDID detailed timing's 16-bit pixel-clock field (at most 655.35 MHz) and 6-bit vertical front
porch cannot hold the panel's 3456x2234 120 Hz timing (1042.13 MHz, front porch 118); a DisplayID
2.0 extension carries the real 120 Hz timing as its preferred timing, with the display
parameters; DRM modes still come from the DCP firmware, not from this EDID (no mode is added,
tested); edid-decode and libdisplay-info both report the EDID conformant; the KUnit fixture uses
the atomic connector state helpers. Then the per-commit build, run.sh and KUnit at the head.

